{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California application screening fee cap and receipts","requirement":"A landlord or agent may charge an application screening fee only up to $30 per applicant (CPI-adjusted), must offer one of the specified screening processes, provide an itemized receipt, return unused amounts, and not charge when no unit is available.","key_value":"$30 per applicant; CPI adjusted annually beginning 1998-01-01","coverage_conditions":"Applies to owners of residential rental property and their agents; applicant includes prospective tenant, guarantor, or cosigner. Federal or state housing assistance program rules are not preempted.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental property applicants; landlord means owner."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"In no case shall the amount of the application screening fee charged by the landlord or their agent be greater than thirty dollars ($30) per applicant. The thirty dollar ($30) application screening fee may be adjusted annually by the landlord or their agent commensurate with an increase in the Consumer Price Index, beginning on January 1, 1998.","interaction":"Does not preempt federal or state housing assistance program rules governing collection of deposits and fees.","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D026-01","doc_id":"D026","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California application screening order and criteria","requirement":"A landlord offering an application screening process must provide screening criteria in writing, consider completed applications in the order received, approve the first qualified applicant, and refund the fee within 7 days if an application is not considered.","key_value":"First qualified applicant approved; criteria in writing","coverage_conditions":"Applies to owners of residential rental property and their agents; applicant includes prospective tenant, guarantor, or cosigner.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Residential rental property applicants; landlord means owner."},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-01-01","citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.6","quoted_span":"(i) Completed applications are considered, as provided for in the landlord’s established screening criteria, in the order in which the completed applications were received. The landlord’s screening criteria shall be provided to the applicant in writing together with the application form.\n(ii) The first applicant who meets the landlord’s established screening criteria is approved for tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
